# Frontend environment (Expo). Copy to `.env.local` and adjust.
#
# - Only EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed vars are exposed to the app.
# - They are INLINED into the JS bundle at build time (not secret).
# - Restart Metro after changing them:  npx expo start -c
#
# Expo loads, in order: .env.local → .env.<mode> → .env  (.env.local wins).

# --- API base URL ---
# Leave UNSET to auto-detect (recommended for local dev):
#   iOS simulator    → http://localhost:8080
#   Android emulator → http://10.0.2.2:8080
#   physical device  → your Mac's LAN IP, derived from the Metro host
# Set it only to force a specific host, e.g. a deployed backend or a fixed LAN IP:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.teamora.example.com
